{"type":"exercise","type_name":"Exercise","number":"","title":"C1","title_html":"C1","html":"<p>The updates <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"eq-add-reml-update\">@eq-add-reml-update</span> are a\nfixed-point iteration, not a descent method, and they are not guaranteed\nto converge from every start. Construct a two-term model in which the\nrestricted likelihood has a stationary point at <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"\\tau_1^2=0\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D70F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.288em; margin-left: -0.08em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\" style=\"margin-left: 0.19em;\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 0.18em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c3D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> (the term is smoothed away),\nverify that this is a fixed point of <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"eq-add-reml-update\">@eq-add-reml-update</span>, and explain\nhow a run that lands there should be reported.</p>","file":"ch44-additive-models/05-structured-additive.html"}